<p>Owens Cross Roads properties often have significant tree coverage — it's part of the area's appeal. But those trees constantly drop debris into your gutters. Pine needles year-round. Leaves every fall. Seeds, twigs, and organic matter throughout the year.</p>

<p>Without protection, you're either cleaning gutters 3-4 times a year yourself or paying someone $150-200+ per cleaning. And out here, finding contractors willing to make regular service calls can be challenging.</p>

<p>Gutter guards solve the problem permanently. They keep debris out while letting water through, reducing maintenance from multiple cleanings yearly to once every few years.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Gutter guards are protective covers that fit over or inside your gutters, blocking debris while allowing water to enter. Different types work better for different debris challenges.</p>

<p>Micro-mesh guards use fine screens that block even pine needles. Screen guards handle larger leaves effectively. Solid covers use surface tension to pull water in while debris slides off. We assess your specific situation and recommend the best solution.</p>
{% endset %}

